        "text": "Finally, you can use a portfolio tracker to manage your crypto portfolio. A portfolio tracker is a program or service that allows you to trace the movements of your holdings. You can see how your current allocation stacks up with your long term goals and track your progress. Some popular trackers include CoinMarketCap, CoinGecko and Delta. To summarize, each investor or trader will have their own ideas on what makes a well balanced crypto portfolio, but here are some general rules worth considering. 1. Split your portfolio between high, medium and low risk investments and give them appropriate weightings. A portfolio containing a large portion of high risk investments is definitely not balanced. It might have the chance to provide you bigger gains, but may also cause huge losses. Your risk profile will determine what's best for you, but there should be some mix.",
